.TH LEO-WRITER 1 "September 2026" "leo-writer 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
leo-writer \- browse an existing NEO Library with LEO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B leo-writer
.RI [ library ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LEO opens an existing NEO Library in a native desktop window. The Library is
read-only in this release. Opening it does not convert or write Library files.
.PP
If no path is given, LEO opens the user's
.I Documents/NEO Library
when it exists. Otherwise, LEO asks the user to choose a Library directory.
.PP
Repeated launches reuse the running LEO process when desktop IPC is available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v , \-\-version
Show the installed version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/leo-writer/leo-writer.log
Application error log when \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR is unset. The Help menu opens
the log in the desktop's default text viewer.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/leo-writer/leo-writer.log
Application error log when \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR is set to an absolute path.
.SH UPDATES
The Help menu checks GitHub Releases for the latest LEO version. It does not
download or install packages. Download the Debian package from the release page,
then install or upgrade it with \fBapt install ./leo-writer_<version>_amd64.deb\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project releases: https://github.com/soubarnak/leo/releases
